  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "The evidence strongly identifies scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile + transformer as the best-performing configuration space (config_028: 0.725, config_008: 0.721). The only remaining untested configuration within this proven encoder pair is config_036 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat). While the pattern (avgpool+weighted=0.706, transformer+weighted=0.725, transformer+concat=0.721) suggests avgpool+concat will likely land around 0.69–0.71 and not surpass 0.725, it is the closest untested configuration to the proven best and completes the 2×2 aggregation×fusion matrix for this encoder pair, reducing residual uncertainty about whether the transformer aggregation gain is robust or partly a fusion-interaction artifact. All other untested options swap to a clearly inferior encoder (resnet50, scgpt) or singleprofile, which showed large performance drops (0.52–0.53). Expected relative cost is moderate (~4–5 GPU hours, comparable to config_020's 4.82 h), since it uses avgpool rather than transformer aggregation. As the final experiment, this is the most informative remaining test within the top-performing design space."
}

